For `globals` I'm not sure.  Documentation [says](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#eval):
> If the globals dictionary is present and does not contain a value for the key `__builtins__`, a reference to the dictionary of the built-in module [builtins](https://docs.python.org/3/library/builtins.html#module-builtins) is inserted under that key before source is parsed.

It's not hard to relax constraint on the `globals` type (see patch below), but this may lead to less useful error messages:
```pycon
>>> d = frozendict({'word': 'hello', '__builtins__': globals()['__builtins__']})
>>> eval('word', globals=d)
'hello'
>>> eval('word', globals=frozendict({'word': 'hello'}))
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "<python-input-2>", line 1, in <module>
    eval('word', globals=frozendict({'word': 'hello'}))
    ~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
TypeError: 'frozendict' object does not support item assignment
```

So, if frozendict does make sense here - any Mapping too.

