Introducing recursive `.register()` calls (bubbling it up to the root class) allows for check like this without iterating over `cls.__subclasses__()`:
```python
from abc import ABC

class Root(ABC):
  pass

class Direct(Root):
  pass

class Registrant:
  pass

Direct.register(Registrant)

assert issubclass(Registrant, Root)
```

