It makes deferred annotations blind to the class scope.

The unhashable cell in your reproduction is the transient class dict cell used in the annotation scope to resolve symbols in the class scope on the annotation level. The default `__annotate__` functions of methods always consume `__classdict__`, so this regression will now reproduce everytime we try hash an annotationlib forward reference from any annotation in a method, because (1) this cell always appears (2) forward references are produced when eager resolution fails.

