[PyInitConfig_Create()](https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/init_config.html#c.PyInitConfig_Create) creates a new initialization configuration using [**Isolated Configuration**](https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/init_config.html#init-isolated-conf) default values, whereas [PyConfig_InitPythonConfig()](https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/init_config.html#c.PyConfig_InitPythonConfig) initializes the configuration with the [**Python Configuration**](https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/init_config.html#init-python-config).

You're seeing differences between the Isolated and the Python configurations. If you want to use `PyInitConfig_Create()` and get the Python configuration, you have to enable explicitly each option. Examples:

```c
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "isolated", 0) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "configure_locale", 1) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "parse_argv", 1) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "user_site_directory", 1) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "safe_path", 0) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
  if (PyInitConfig_SetInt (config, "install_signal_handlers", 1) < 0) {
    goto error;
  }
```

You may only pick the options which fit your use case, you may not need all of them.

> In the diff below, you can see that the configuration dump has a lot of differences, and the setting of use_environment failed (0 instead of 1).

The Isolated Configuration sets `isolated` option to `1` which overrides `safe_path`, `use_environment` and `user_site_directory`: https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/init_config.html#c.PyConfig.isolated

